1... Nf6 {Flexible. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
2. c4 {Space. The pawn on c4 controls d5.}
2... e6 {Solid. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
3. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
3... b6 {[%csl Gb7] The Queen's Indian.}
4. g3 {Fianchetto.}
4... Ba6 {Hits c4. The bishop on a6 eyes the pawn on c4.}
 (4... Bb7 {Classical development. The bishop on b7 eyes the knight on f3 and controls d5 and e4.}
5. Bg2 {Long diagonal.}
5... Be7 {Develops.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
)
5. b3 {Defends c4.}
5... Bb4+ {Checks. It is check, so the reply is forced.}
6. Bd2 {Blocks. The bishop on d2 eyes the bishop on b4.}
6... Be7 {Retreats.}
7. Bg2 {Long diagonal.}
7... c6 {Prepares ...d5. The pawn on c6 controls d5.}
8. Bc3 {Develops.}
8... d5 {Centre. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls e4.}
9. Ne5 {Central. The knight on e5 eyes the pawn on f7 and the pawn on c6.}
9... Nfd7 {Challenges. The knight on d7 eyes the knight on e5.} *

